---
const masks = [
  [false, true, false, true],
  [false, true, false, true],
  [false, true, false, true],
  [false, false, true, true],
  [false, false, true, true],
  [false, false, true, true]
];
---

<figure class="project-figure amelia-mechanism">
  <div class="mechanism-steps">
    <div class="mechanism-step">
      <span class="mechanism-number">1</span>
      <h3>Group the missingness</h3>
      <div class="missingness-grid" aria-hidden="true">
        {
          masks.map((row, index) => (
            <div class:list={["missingness-row", { "pattern-break": index === 3 }]}>
              {row.map((missing) => (
                <span class:list={{ missing }} />
              ))}
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p>Rows with the same missing variables share a conditional covariance calculation.</p>
      <p class="mechanism-legend">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span> Observed <span class="missing-key" aria-hidden="true"
        ></span> Missing
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mechanism-step mechanism-compute">
      <span class="mechanism-number">2</span>
      <h3>Compute with matrices</h3>
      <div class="matrix-operations">
        <p><span>E-step</span> Conditional means + uncertainty</p>
        <p
          class="matrix-formula"
          aria-label="Y transpose times Y, plus conditional covariance corrections"
        >
          Y<sup>T</sup>Y + C
        </p>
        <p><span>M-step</span> Update the mean and covariance</p>
      </div>
      <p>
        PyTorch can run these matrix operations across GPU cores. Large row groups provide work to
        share.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mechanism-step">
      <span class="mechanism-number">3</span>
      <h3>Check, repeat, draw</h3>
      <div class="iteration-loop" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Estimate</span><span>→</span><span>Check</span>
        <span class="loop-return">Repeat until convergence</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Each EM iteration depends on the last. Then draw missing values and repeat for another
        bootstrap sample.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mechanism-boundary">
    <strong>The complete call still matters.</strong>
    <span
      >CPU preparation → device transfer → matrix work → synchronization and returned results</span
    >
    <p>
      Transfers and small operations add overhead. Imputation replicas currently run one at a time;
      the R compatibility route keeps all steps outside EM in R.
    </p>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="project-caption">
    Conceptual view of the implementation. Y contains observed values and conditional means; C
    retains the uncertainty in missing values. GPU parallelism occurs within matrix operations,
    while the statistical sequence is preserved. The relative cost of each stage has not yet been
    profiled.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .mechanism-steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }
  .mechanism-step {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .mechanism-step h3 {
    margin: 0.65rem 0 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .mechanism-step p {
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }
  .mechanism-number {
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .missingness-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    max-width: 10rem;
    height: 8.5rem;
    align-content: center;
  }
  .missingness-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .missingness-row span {
    height: 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .missingness-row .missing {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-style: dashed;
  }
  .pattern-break {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .mechanism-step .mechanism-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .mechanism-legend span {
    width: 0.65rem;
    height: 0.65rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .mechanism-legend .missing-key {
    margin-left: 0.4rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-style: dashed;
  }
  .matrix-operations {
    display: grid;
    align-content: center;
    min-height: 8.5rem;
    padding: 0.7rem;
    background: var(--sky-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .matrix-operations p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
  .matrix-operations span {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .matrix-operations .matrix-formula {
    margin: 0.55rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
  }
  .iteration-loop {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto auto auto;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-content: center;
    min-height: 8.5rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .loop-return {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--accent);
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
  .mechanism-boundary {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .mechanism-boundary strong,
  .mechanism-boundary span {
    display: block;
  }
  .mechanism-boundary span {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
  }
  .mechanism-boundary p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .mechanism-steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .mechanism-step + .mechanism-step {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding-top: 1.25rem;
    }
    .mechanism-step h3 {
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }
    .missingness-grid {
      height: auto;
    }
    .matrix-operations,
    .iteration-loop {
      min-height: auto;
      max-width: 23rem;
    }
  }
</style>
